Dark Age

We have entered an age of unprecedented connectedness, with a high frequency of seemingly-major news events every day, and the destruction of the internet with a flood of machine-generated content. This comes at a time when right-wing sentiments world over are at a peak, and the leader is rapidly declining, and thrashing about in denial. The situation on the ground is bleak, with essentials like gas and groceries costing a small fortune. The level of human discourse has dropped to sharing small snippets of text to prompt the machine. The very foundations of career progression are being challenged, with people racing to generate large volumes of output using the machine. Academia is not saved either, with research around using the machine drowning everything else out, and respectable academics questioning the very foundations of our academic institutions. The very incentive structure around which human society is built has the single goal of furthering human learning and understanding. The incentive structure is built around useful producing human output as a proxy, and the machine does nothing else but to produce human-like output. The quality of the machine-output is questionable, but it seems to be "good enough" for many to wholly surrender their cognitive functions to it, accepting everything it produces as the truth. Nearly everyone has a childish fascination with the machine that will plunge us into the next Dark Age.
